  body: "# Free in-patient treatment in the JSA and IS guidance\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    guidance requires several conditions together for free in-patient treatment: free maintenance, medical
    or other treatment, a hospital or similar institution, in-patient status and a specified legislative
    or Defence Council basis.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nA hospital address or an NHS label alone is
    insufficient. Private-patient exceptions and the factual meaning of in-patient must be checked. The
    source contains older dated guidance; periods, premiums, current legislation and JSA labour-market
    exceptions remain unresolved. It does not establish that every hospital stay changes an award.\n\n\
    ## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 24007, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f006886650c031ce2c41b/dmgch24.pdf#page=11)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 24: Special cases.\n- [DMG 24008, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f006886650c031ce2c41b/dmgch24.pdf#page=11)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 24: Special cases.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch24`: PDF SHA-256 `2827c11c3ce95e852073142524e0410c6534f7bf140d885be18cad09f6ece98a`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `91863ddf195bf30158383f17cb2653f1ba498551a695c8ec0ba1e138d00a222c`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-hospital-family-membership
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Hospital treatment and continued family membership are separate questions in the
      chapter; the family passage directs the reader to chapter 22 rather than deciding membership
      from admission alone.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch24/0011
      quote: "24007   A person must be in each of the following categories to be receiving free in-patient\n\
        \        treatment\n\n        1.    maintained free of charge\n\n        2.    receiving medical
        or other treatment\n\n        3.    in a hospital or similar institution\n\n        4.    an in-patient\n\
        \n        5.    receiving the treatment\n\n              5.1      under prescribed legislation1
        or\n\n              5.2      in a hospital or similar institution maintained or administered by
        the\n                       Defence Council.\n\n        Note: A person who does not meet any one
        of these conditions is not receiving free\n        in-patient treatment. The DM does not need
        to consider the other conditions.\n                                                          \
        \        1 NHS Act 06; NHS (Scot) Act 78; NHS & CC Act 90\n\n        Maintained free of charge"
      locator: DMG 24007
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch24/0025
      quote: "24097   The DM should consider the guidance in DMG Chapter 22 to decide whether a\n    \
        \    patient is still a member of a family if the patient is a\n\n        1.      lone parent
        or\n\n        2.      member of a couple or\n\n        3.      member of a polygamous marriage\n\
        \n        4.      a child or young person.\n\n\n\n\nVol 4 Amendment 22 June 2007"
      locator: DMG 24097
